  "summary": "I reconciled all 5 St. Brigid discharges under RBC-TOC-02 and wrote a progress note for each. Results and documents that arrived while I worked changed decisions for 3 patients; I corrected those and documented why in addendum notes.\n\n**Walter Kim (pt-0005)**\n- Furosemide changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily, following the signed addendum (mr-t0001).\n- Potassium chloride stopped, per the discharge summary.\n- Lisinopril: at first I kept it on hold because potassium was 5.4 on 10/21. A repeat panel arrived (10/23: K 4.7, creatinine 1.21), which meets the discharge condition for restarting, so I resumed the existing lisinopril 10 mg order (mr-00072).\n- Please disregard task-t0003, the potassium-review task I made before the repeat result came in. The system wouldn't let me cancel it.\n- An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg twice daily arrived. Only signed addenda count, so I didn't act on it.\n- Omeprazole kept as his home drug; pantoprazole was only a hospital formulary swap, so I didn't order it.\n- Metoprolol, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged.\n\n**Terence Stark (pt-0004)**\n- Carvedilol: I first raised it to 12.5 mg twice daily per the discharge summary. A signed addendum then arrived: the increase was reversed before discharge because of a slow heart rate (48–52) and lightheadedness on standing. I changed it back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0017), so the net result is no change from his home dose.\n- **Flagged to you (comm-t0006):** atorvastatin 80 mg. His fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, so he likely isn't taking it as prescribed. Per policy I made no change.\n- **Flagged to you (comm-t0007):** glipizide 5 mg from Dr. Desai at Valley Endocrinology, filled at an outside pharmacy. We have no order for it and the discharge summary doesn't mention it. He is also on insulin 70/30.\n\n**Earnest Roberts (pt-0044)**\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: I resumed it after creatinine was 1.08 on 10/22. A potassium of 5.5 then came in (10/23), so I put it back on hold.\n- **For you:** task-t0018, due 10/26, to review his next potassium and decide on lisinopril.\n- Insulins and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\n**Gerald Whitcomb (pt-0069)**\n- Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (creatinine 1.12, potassium 4.4 on 10/21).\n- The discharge summary also called for a potassium 3 days after discharge, and that result hasn't arrived yet. If it comes back above 5.0, lisinopril should be put back on hold.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\n**Lorraine Pruitt (pt-0067)**\n- Metformin ER is still on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in the hospital, and the restart condition requires a post-discharge result.\n- **For you:** task-t0013, due 10/24, to review the post-discharge metabolic panel and resume her existing metformin order if creatinine is below 1.5.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nI closed the 4 inbox items that arrived during the work, and checked the queues again with nothing new.",
